cts to your LDAP server and custom REST API. Utilizes NFC to \"check in\" wherever you place an NFC tag. Classes include Location, Device, Tag, and Check. A location is a specific place/building in which tags can be located. A device can be anything from a printer to a chair to a paper closet. A tag is a specific NFC tag that is added to the REST API through the app, which collects the tag's uuid and matches it with a specific location, device type, and description. A check happens when in the Check Activity and scan an NFC tag; the scan registers the tag's uuid and matches it to a specific tag in the database, and if it is valid, you can give a certain status and short description of the tag's current state.","topics":[],"score":206236,"global_rank":295111},{"name":"goelakash/QuoraWeb","owner":"goelakash","html_url":"https://github.com/goelakash/QuoraWeb","stars":0,"forks":1,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Java","description":"An simple WebView alternative for Quora on android.","topics":[],"score":206236,"global_rank":295114},{"name":"karan11singla/PostIt","owner":"karan11singla","html_url":"https://github.com/karan11singla/PostIt","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Java","description":null,"topics":[],"score":206232,"global_rank":295141},{"name":"curiousclarissa/ud843_DidYouFeelIt-copied","owner":"curiousclarissa","html_url":"https://github.com/curiousclarissa/ud843_DidYouFeelIt-copied","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Java","description":"back up while learning","topics":[],"score":206232,"global_rank":295152},{"name":"curiousclarissa/Pokemon-copied","owner":"curiousclarissa","html_url":"https://github.com/curiousclarissa/Pokemon-copied","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Java","description":"backed up here for debugging during learning process","topics":[],"score":206232,"global_rank":295153},{"name":"vi-li/Console-Etch-a-Sketch","owner":"vi-li","html_url":"https://github.com/vi-li/Console-Etc